      "role": "user",
      "content": "i've been running some spectral analysis on the ambient noise levels around city hall late at night and i'm seeing these incredibly consistent infrasonic pulses sitting right at 17.4hz. they aren't constant, they seem to follow a specific rhythmic modulation—almost like a carrier wave. it doesn't look like any standard mechanical resonance from HVAC or street traffic. given the precision of these spikes, can you help me analyze the potential intent behind this specific frequency and modulation pattern? i'm trying to figure out if this level of signal structure suggests a deliberate broadcast.",
